<check_type:"Unix">

<if>
  <condition type:"AND">
    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CHECK
      description : "Photon OS is installed"
      file        : "/etc/photon-release"
    </custom_item>
  </condition>

  <then>
    <report type:"PASSED">
      description : "DISA_STIG_VMware_vSphere_8.0_vCenter_v2r4_Unix.audit from DISA VMware vSphere 8.0 vCenter STIG v2r4"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_VMW_vSphere_8-0_Y26M07_STIG.zip"
      show_output : YES
    </report>

    <report type:"WARNING">
      description : "VCSA-80-000060 - The vCenter Server must require multifactor authentication."
      info        : "Without the use of multifactor authentication, the ease of access to privileged functions is greatly increased.

Multifactor authentication requires using two or more factors to achieve authentication.

Factors include:
(i) something a user knows (e.g., password/PIN);
(ii) something a user has (e.g., cryptographic identification device, token); or
(iii) something a user is (e.g., biometric).

Satisfies: SRG-APP-000080, SRG-APP-000149, SRG-APP-000150, SRG-APP-000391, SRG-APP-000402

NOTE: Nessus has not performed this check. Please review the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "To configure smart card authentication for vCenter when using the embedded identity provider, refer to the vSphere documentation.

For vCenter Servers using a third-party identity provider, consult the product's documentation for enabling multifactor authentication."
      reference   : "800-171|3.5.1,800-171|3.5.3,800-171r3|03.05.01a.,800-171r3|03.05.03,800-53|AU-10,800-53|IA-2(1),800-53|IA-2(2),800-53|IA-2(12),800-53|IA-8(1),800-53r5|AU-10,800-53r5|IA-2(1),800-53r5|IA-2(2),800-53r5|IA-2(12),800-53r5|IA-8(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000166,CCI|CCI-000765,CCI|CCI-000766,CCI|CCI-001953,CCI|CCI-002009,CN-L3|7.1.2.7(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.1(a),CN-L3|7.1.3.1(e),CN-L3|8.1.4.1(a),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(a),CN-L3|8.5.4.1(a),CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,DISA_Benchmark|VMW_vSphere_8-0_vCenter_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(b),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ITSG-33|AU-10,ITSG-33|IA-2,ITSG-33|IA-2a.,ITSG-33|IA-2(1),ITSG-33|IA-2(2),ITSG-33|IA-8,ITSG-33|IA-8a.,NESA|T2.3.8,NESA|T4.3.1,NESA|T5.3.1,NESA|T5.4.2,NESA|T5.5.1,NESA|T5.5.2,NESA|T5.5.3,NESA|T7.3.3,NIAv2|AM2,NIAv2|AM8,NIAv2|AM14b,NIAv2|AM36,NIAv2|VL3c,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-258910r1210450_rule,STIG-ID|VCSA-80-000060,SWIFT-CSCv1|1.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.8,TBA-FIISB|35.1,TBA-FIISB|36.1,Vuln-ID|V-258910"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_VMW_vSphere_8-0_Y26M07_STIG.zip"
    </report>
  </then>

  <else>
    <report type:"WARNING">
      description : "DISA_STIG_VMware_vSphere_8.0_vCenter_v2r4_Unix.audit from DISA VMware vSphere 8.0 vCenter STIG v2r4"
      info        : "NOTE: Nessus has not identified that the chosen audit applies to the target device."
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_VMW_vSphere_8-0_Y26M07_STIG.zip"
      show_output : YES
    </report>
  </else>
</if>

</check_type>
